#################################################################

#################################################################
#  v9.62.0, second block -- CORRECTION FOUND BY THE FIRST READING.
#  The restart (v9.61.0) flagged only the 14 bypassed items. The
#  retraction of lineage 7's chain also un-orders the other 24: the
#  Backlog output they were ordered against is retracted, so the
#  order check read the parent as BYPASS (38 items, no active Backlog
#  output). A restart retracts the chain that ordered EVERY item, so
#  every item of the restarted lineage is pre-lineage from then on and
#  re-enters only by admission. Corrected here, before any part output
#  exists: the 22 items that belong to a deliverable (directly, or as
#  the execution task of a story that does) go to that deliverable's
#  part; the initiative and the spike, which pursue the framework-wide
#  conformance objective and belong to no single deliverable, stay with
#  the parent and will be admitted by its combine output.
#################################################################

