#################################################################
#  v9.69.0 (2026-09-09, brsf-session) -- THE IMPEDIMENT CLEARS. The two
#  external decisions Imp_RegisterPackageDecisions waited on since
#  2026-09-03 were made once the proposals were delivered (v1.202.0):
#    configuration:RoadmapReportConvention  -- OE, configuration_abox v2.7.0
#       (oe-pack v20.59.0; one correction to the proposed parent class,
#       ProjectMarkdownDocument, not EngineeringArtefact)
#    prof:RoadmapReportKind                 -- another registrant, rdodi_profiles_abox
#       v1.2.0 (two corrections of another registrant's own)
#  Both read directly from the ratifying ABoxes at origin, not from the
#  log lines. hasProposalStatus is a current-state pointer and is moved
#  Prop_Submitted -> Prop_Accepted in place (L-112); this note is the
#  history. The RegisterPackage can now be honestly built, and is.
#################################################################
fw:EnhProp_RoadmapReportConvention backlog:hasRationale "Accepted 2026-09-07 by OE (configuration_abox v2.7.0, oe-pack v20.59.0): configuration:RoadmapReportConvention exists, filenamePattern {name}_v{M}_{m}_{p}.md, dcterms:source citing this framework's proposal." .
fw:EnhProp_RoadmapReportKind backlog:hasRationale "Accepted 2026-09-08 by another registrant (rdodi_profiles_abox v1.2.0): prof:RoadmapReportKind exists as a doc:ArtifactKindSpec." .

#################################################################
#  THE REGISTER PACKAGE. Built from the ratified conventions:
#    - register data: this file, under configuration:ABoxFileConvention
#    - profile declaration: the AdoptionProfile lives in this same file
#      (one file, two roles; each RegisterArtifact carries one role)
#    - progress report: the FIRST retained roadmap report run, written
#      by backlog_roadmap_report_v1_6_0 on register v9.68.0 and kept as
#      04-documentation/roadmap_report_run_v1_239_0.md under
#      configuration:RoadmapReportConvention (its kind: prof:RoadmapReportKind)
#    - manifest: MANIFEST_SHA256.txt. Its own SHA-256 cannot be recorded
#      inside a file the manifest covers (the register), because the
#      manifest would then have to cover its own digest -- no fixed
#      point exists. The value below is the digest of the manifest AS
#      PUBLISHED at v1.238.0 (commit 9a85c64), a real, checkable
#      historical digest; the digest of each release's manifest is
#      carried outside the manifest's coverage by the publisher
#      (PUBLISH_RECORD.ttl, manifestVerified/manifestTotal) and by the
#      release tag. Stated, not hidden (G7).
#################################################################

#################################################################
#  OE'S ADJUDICATION ON THE RISK-FACET PROPOSAL, APPLIED (ADJUDICATION_
#  OE_to_backlog-roadmap-framework_risk-facet-registration_v1_0_0, 2026-09-08).
#  Not risk:hasIdentifiedRisk (risk = prospective uncertainty; these
#  findings are confirmed, retrospective facts) but quality:hasFinding
#  from a quality:QualityAssessment this register mints, each finding
#  multi-typed quality:Finding alongside its own RetrospectiveFinding
#  type -- using OE's classes to type our individuals, not minting
#  OE vocabulary (B1). 43 findings.
#################################################################
fw:Find_ChangelogHeaderLoss a quality:Finding .
fw:Find_MissingFixtureCaseName a quality:Finding .
fw:Find_SelfReferentialProofPath a quality:Finding .
fw:Find_SymmetricDivergenceRule a quality:Finding .
# the run also names this register's own ReportSection individuals (fw:RS_*, keyed to the same nine sections the tool emits as backlog:Section_*)

#################################################################
#  v9.70.0 (2026-09-09, brsf-session) -- THE MANIFEST DIGEST, SOLVED
#  RATHER THAN WORKED AROUND (owner's decision 3). The digest of a
#  covered set lives outside the set. RELEASE_METRICS.txt is manifest-
#  exempt and is written from the manifest bytes before any gate runs;
#  the manifest artifact names it as carrier; the gate verifies the
#  carrier is exempt and current; the publisher hashes the gate
#  transcript into the publish record. The v9.69.0 hasManifestSHA256
#  value stays as the historical record it was declared to be.
#################################################################

#################################################################
#  2026-09-09T12:02:15Z -- ARCHIVAL by backlog_lineage_archive_v1_0_0: 574 subjects of
#  L_OntologyDriven, L7_Gov, L7_Exec, L7_Export, L7_Prose, L7_Code, L_ChangeDiscipline set down into 01-ontologies/backlog_framework_archive_abox_v1_1_0.ttl; the lineage,
#  its mission and its closure report stay here as the record that points in.
#################################################################


#################################################################
#  v9.72.0 (2026-09-09, brsf-session) -- LINEAGE STATUS on every
#  lineage (TBox v1.89.0): archived lineages 1-6 and, from this
#  release, 7 (with its five parts) and 8 are LS_Archived (the
#  archive tool stamped the latter). Read from the register, not
#  asserted from memory.
#################################################################

#################################################################
#  v9.72.0 -- LINEAGE 9, Mission stage, RECORDED FOR REAL. v1.242.0's
#  changelog claimed this stage; the snippet that carried it had been
#  truncated to zero bytes by the session's own script, and the
#  register at 5f8b318 contains none of it. That claim was false and
#  is corrected here: the Mission stage's witnessed commit is this
#  one, not 5f8b318. Nothing is re-dated. Status: LS_Opened.
#################################################################
fw:L_SDLCObligations a backlog:Lineage ; rdfs:label "Lineage 9"@en ;
    backlog:lineageForMission fw:Mission_SDLCObligations ;
    backlog:lineageOrdinal 14 ;
    backlog:lineageArchived false ;
    backlog:hasLineageStatus backlog:LS_Backlogged .   # moved in place at each stage (L-112); the chain of stage outputs is the history
fw:Mission_SDLCObligations a backlog:Mission ;
    backlog:producedByStage fw:Out_Mission_SDLC ;
    backlog:hasMissionStatement "The lineage is connected to the software development life cycle as its mandatory facilities: each stage of the Mission-Scope-Goal-Objective-Backlog chain declares the engineering artifacts it owes -- domain entities and blueprint at Scope, use cases with main and alternative scenarios at Goal, activity and sequence diagrams at Objective, the domain-class model and blueprint gaps at Backlog, and the ISO 12207 task types' artifacts at execution -- and no stage output closes, no refinement counts, and no item reaches Done without the owed artifacts existing, witnessed by git before the output that claims them. Enforced by shapes and the order check, proven on fixtures, and run first on this lineage itself." ;
    backlog:missionFor fw:Register ;
    backlog:hasMissionOrigin backlog:Origin_OwnerStated ;
    backlog:missionSource "Owner, 2026-09-09, verbatim: 'The lineage had a Mission, Scope, Goals and Objectives -- but no Blueprint and no DomainEntity individuals. The more critical point is that how the domain engineering, analysis, design, implementation, testing, modeling, documentation are connected with the lineage. As far as we have mechanisms for the execution of the lineage steps but cannot force them to build certain artifacts. For example, grooming doesn't have any enforcement to define the use cases, their main and alternative scenarios, drawing activity diagrams, sequence diagrams, discover the domain classes, etc. This means we are not correctly connect the lineage with SDLC to guarantee the related engineering tasks to explore, define, model, and develop specifications for them.' and, on the four-point design: 'SDLC obligation design seems fine for me. Can you build it?'" ;
    backlog:hasMissionOutcome backlog:Out_InFlight ;
    backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner .
fw:Out_Mission_SDLC a backlog:StageOutput ;
    backlog:outputOfStage backlog:Stage_Mission ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_SDLCObligations ;
    backlog:hasStateDigest "c4ef20cf8495bd8d37dc9cca6cdef0247178396a2acdf074e9016e3d241a656c" ;
    backlog:closedAtCommit "backlog-roadmap-framework-v1.243.0 (tag; witnessed by git, not asserted)" ;
    backlog:hasRationale "Mission stage of lineage 9 closed with the mission alone on the record. The first attempt to record it (v1.242.0) shipped an empty snippet; this is the real one." .

#################################################################
#  v9.72.0 (2026-09-09, brsf-session) -- LINEAGE 9, Scope stage.
#  Consumes Out_Mission_SDLC (6b00dd9). Status moves to LS_Scoped in this commit. Under the obligations this
#  lineage introduces, the Scope stage owes the DOMAIN ENTITIES and
#  the BLUEPRINT of its own domain before its output may close --
#  produced here, in this commit, before Out_Scope_SDLC.
#################################################################
fw:Scope_SDLCObligations a backlog:ScopeStatement ;
    backlog:hasScopeStatementText "Connect the lineage to the SDLC as mandatory facilities, in four parts: (1) stage obligations -- each pipeline stage declares the artifact kinds it owes, drawn from another registrant's artifact-kind specifications; (2) closure requires the owed artifacts, witnessed -- a StageOutput closes only when ArtifactEvidence of every owed kind exists for the lineage and first appears in git before the output; (3) refinement produces or does not count -- a PlanningEvent on an epic or story produces the use-case and scenario artifacts for the items it plans; (4) enforcement at Done -- the owed artifact kinds of an item's task type join its effective Definition of Done. Proven on a positive and a negative fixture, measured by the order check, and run first on this lineage." ;
    backlog:scopeForMission fw:Mission_SDLCObligations ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_Derived ;
    backlog:producedByStage fw:Out_Scope_SDLC ;
    backlog:requiresDeliverable fw:Del_StageObligations , fw:Del_WitnessedClosure , fw:Del_RefinementProduces , fw:Del_DoDArtifacts ;
    backlog:coversArea fw:Area_SDLC_Vocabulary , fw:Area_SDLC_Shapes , fw:Area_SDLC_Witness , fw:Area_SDLC_Fixtures ;
    backlog:hasScopeExclusion fw:Ex_SDLC_NoNewKinds , fw:Ex_SDLC_NoRetrofit ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_SDLCObligations .
fw:Area_SDLC_Vocabulary a backlog:ScopeArea ; backlog:areaMeasure "Zero stage-obligation properties exist in backlog_tbox_v1_89_0 (grep stageOwes: 0; refinementProduces: 0); ArtifactEvidence exists (v1.8x) with no kind typing from prof:. Counted 2026-09-09." ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ; backlog:areaLocation "01-ontologies/backlog_tbox -- stageOwesArtifactKind, refinementProduces, artifact-evidence typing" ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_SDLCObligations .
fw:Area_SDLC_Shapes a backlog:ScopeArea ; backlog:areaMeasure "Zero shapes in backlog_shacl_v1_110_0 condition a StageOutput's closure, a PlanningEvent's validity, or an item's Done on an owed artifact (grep owed/ArtifactKind: 0). EpicPlanningShape is the one artifact obligation that exists (coversEntity). Counted 2026-09-09." ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ; backlog:areaLocation "02-shacl-safeguards/backlog_shacl -- stage-closure, refinement and DoD obligation shapes" ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_SDLCObligations .
fw:Area_SDLC_Witness a backlog:ScopeArea ; backlog:areaMeasure "backlog_lineage_order_check_v1_4_0 measures the order of stage outputs and items only; zero artifact-before-output measurements. Counted 2026-09-09." ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ; backlog:areaLocation "03-tooling/backlog_lineage_order_check -- artifact-before-output measurement" ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_SDLCObligations .
fw:Area_SDLC_Fixtures a backlog:ScopeArea ; backlog:areaMeasure "Zero fixtures under 03-tooling/fixtures name a stage obligation (grep sdlc_obligation: 0) out of 62 fixtures. Counted 2026-09-09." ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ; backlog:areaLocation "03-tooling/fixtures -- fixture_sdlc_obligations (positive) and fixture_sdlc_obligations_negative" ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_SDLCObligations .
fw:Del_StageObligations a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; backlog:deliverableForArea fw:Area_SDLC_Vocabulary ;
    backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "each stage of the Mission-Scope-Goal-Objective-Backlog chain declares the engineering artifacts it owes" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_SDLCObligations .
fw:Del_WitnessedClosure a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; backlog:deliverableForArea fw:Area_SDLC_Shapes ;
    backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "no stage output closes ... without the owed artifacts existing, witnessed by git before the output that claims them" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_SDLCObligations .
fw:Del_RefinementProduces a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; backlog:deliverableForArea fw:Area_SDLC_Shapes ;
    backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "no refinement counts ... without the owed artifacts existing" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_SDLCObligations .
fw:Del_DoDArtifacts a backlog:ScopeDeliverable ; backlog:deliverableForArea fw:Area_SDLC_Shapes ;
    backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Product ;
    backlog:derivesFromMissionClause "no item reaches Done without the owed artifacts existing" ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_SDLCObligations .
fw:Ex_SDLC_NoNewKinds a backlog:ScopeExclusion ;
    backlog:excludesConcern "Minting artifact-kind vocabulary of this framework's own (use case, scenario, activity diagram, sequence diagram, domain model, test specification, ...). another registrant's prof: ArtifactKindSpecs already define these; the stage obligations reference them by IRI. A kind another registrant lacks is proposed to another registrant's inbox, not minted here." ;
    backlog:hasExclusionRationale "L-64: the vocabulary belongs to the subject that owns it. prof:RoadmapReportKind was obtained exactly this way in Imp_RegisterPackageDecisions; the same road is taken for every kind this lineage needs." ;
    backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_SDLCObligations .
fw:Ex_SDLC_NoRetrofit a backlog:ScopeExclusion ;
    backlog:excludesConcern "Applying the new obligations to lineages already closed or archived (1-8) and to the toy lineages of the exercise register. Their outputs were closed under the rules in force; a closed chain reopened to produce artifacts it never owed is a backfill." ;
    backlog:hasExclusionRationale "G41 and L-112: closed history is a record. Obligations bind lineages opened after they ship, and this lineage itself." ;
    backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner ; backlog:hasScopeLayer backlog:Layer_Work ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_SDLCObligations .

# --- what the Scope stage OWES under its own rule: the domain entities and the blueprint of this domain ---
fw:Blueprint_SDLCObligations a backlog:Blueprint ; backlog:blueprintFor fw:Register ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_SDLCObligations ;
    backlog:hasRationale "Blueprint of the stage-obligation domain: five entities, each to be carried through creation, active use, suspension/exception and termination by the work of this lineage. Produced at the Scope stage because that is what the Scope stage owes (Del_StageObligations, point 1 of the scope)." .
fw:Entity_StageObligation a backlog:DomainEntity ; rdfs:label "Stage obligation"@en ; rdfs:comment "A pipeline stage's declaration of the artifact kinds it owes before its output may close."@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_SDLCObligations .
fw:Entity_OwedArtifactKind a backlog:DomainEntity ; rdfs:label "Owed artifact kind"@en ; rdfs:comment "An artifact kind (a prof: ArtifactKindSpec) named by a stage obligation or a task-type obligation."@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_SDLCObligations .
fw:Entity_ArtifactEvidence a backlog:DomainEntity ; rdfs:label "Artifact evidence"@en ; rdfs:comment "A produced artifact of an owed kind, tied to a lineage and witnessed by git before the output that claims it."@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_SDLCObligations .
fw:Entity_RefinementProduct a backlog:DomainEntity ; rdfs:label "Refinement product"@en ; rdfs:comment "The use-case and scenario artifacts a PlanningEvent produces for the items it plans."@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_SDLCObligations .
fw:Entity_TaskTypeObligation a backlog:DomainEntity ; rdfs:label "Task-type obligation"@en ; rdfs:comment "The artifact kinds an ISO 12207 task type owes at execution, joining the item's effective Definition of Done."@en ; backlog:belongsToLineage fw:L_SDLCObligations .
